{
 "rr-src": {
  "text": "Your referral process is facts paper, voicemail, and prayer. That's not a workflow. That's a hostage situation. Every GP is different. An email here, a call there, a sticky note somewhere. Hell, the patient just waits. Now check out tooth referral. Here's what it does. Every incoming referral from every office lands in one list. Each office gets a green dot once it's connected. Build that network once and referrals just flow in. Click one. The diagnosis, the tooth numbers, and what they want done are all there. No detective work is required. Do you need a better x-ray? Message the referring office right inside the case. They answer like adults. Update the status, schedule the consult, and the GP is notified. There's zero phone tag and zero just checking in emails. That's what a referral network should feel like. Connected offices, one place, and nobody left guessing. Want to see it for yourself? Check out tooth referral and start connecting your referral network.",
